NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.13.1 (crates.io): a CancelToken can be
made over an existing flag (CancelToken::from_flag) and can poll a
condition with it (with_check), so a request's interrupt flag and its
time and memory limits stop a boolean from inside; and the largest step
of a boolean's result assembly, AddNewEdgeVerts, allocates its lists at
their final size and checks the token as it fills them and between its
sorts. Without a token nothing changes, and with one that never fires
the output is unchanged. Tests: crates/geom/tests/kernel_cancel.rs and
crates/web/test/run.mjs (the Menger sponge at depth 5 under 1 GiB).

Apply from the crate root on top of 0005: patch -p1 < this file. The
crate's sources use CRLF line endings.
See vendor/README.md ("The cancellation patch").
